From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yoshisto Yanagisawa <yyanagisawa@chromium.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:27:13 -0700
Subject: [Workers] Plumb SanitizeScriptErrors state through worker error
 reporting

Previously, ExecutionContext::DispatchErrorEvent() passed the
SanitizeScriptErrors parameter to DispatchErrorEventInternal() for local
event dispatch, but did not forward it to ExceptionThrown() or retain it
for exceptions queued in pending_exceptions_.

This change threads SanitizeScriptErrors through
ExecutionContext::ExceptionThrown() and WorkerReportingProxy::ReportException()
so that worker reporting proxies (DedicatedWorkerMessagingProxy,
SharedWorkerReportingProxy, and ServiceWorkerGlobalScopeProxy) have
direct access to the sanitization state when constructing and reporting
error events across threads.

Additionally:
- Store SanitizeScriptErrors alongside each ErrorEvent in
  ExecutionContext::pending_exceptions_ to maintain state across nested
  error event dispatches.
- Guard the updated parent-side reporting behavior behind the
  SanitizeWorkerErrorPropagation runtime enabled feature flag.

TAG=agy
CONV=374fa867-5861-40a0-be10-1c8d1a60722d

Bug: 501901218
Change-Id: I3ccce9b1ba81a058dde9843a267631b0fb0399f9
