Auto-Submit: Yoshisato Yanagisawa <yyanagisawa@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Hiroki Nakagawa <nhiroki@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Hiroki Nakagawa <nhiroki@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1721579}

Electron adaptation notes (45-x-y): execution_context.cc/.h conflicted with the branch's [M156] 'Avoid re-entry when draining pending error events' (is_draining_pending_exceptions_ guard, which this CL predates). Resolved to the same text as upstream main after both changes: pending_exceptions_ becomes HeapVector<std::pair<Member<ErrorEvent>, SanitizeScriptErrors>>, ExceptionThrown() receives the per-event SanitizeScriptErrors, and the branch's base::AutoReset draining guard, std::move() of the pending list and CHECK(pending_exceptions_.empty()) are kept. All other files applied cleanly.

Electron's PreloadRealmGlobalScope (feat_add_preloadrealmglobalscope.patch) also overrides ExceptionThrown(); its override takes the new SanitizeScriptErrors argument and forwards it to the initiator context.

